The anydoc R package is released under the MIT license (see LICENSE).

The package links a Rust static library. Its sources are not shipped in this
tarball -- they are downloaded at build time as a checksum-verified archive
(tools/vendor.R) -- but the installed shared object contains their compiled
code, so their licenses apply to the installed package.

All 140 crates are distributed under permissive licenses. The full list, with
each crate's version, license and declared authors, is in inst/AUTHORS.

Most offer MIT as one option. The following do not, and are redistributed
under the terms shown:

  ryu 1.0.23        Apache-2.0 OR BSL-1.0
  zopfli 0.8.3      Apache-2.0
  zlib-rs 0.6.7     Zlib

Two crates carry conjunctive terms, where the second component applies in
addition to the choice offered by the first:

  encoding_rs 0.8.35     (Apache-2.0 OR MIT) AND BSD-3-Clause
  unicode-ident 1.0.24   (MIT OR Apache-2.0) AND Unicode-3.0

The upstream 'anydoc' Rust crate itself (https://github.com/firecrawl/anydoc)
is MIT licensed, copyright Firecrawl.
